33
00:01:34.583 --> 00:01:35.677
Fall over!

34
00:01:36.577 --> 00:01:38.614
Fall over. Your turn!

35
00:01:41.514 --> 00:01:42.840
Fall over!

36
00:01:43.140 --> 00:01:44.165
Excellent!

37
00:01:45.150 --> 00:01:54.634
Emergency number, Emergency number! Ambulance call, Ambulance call! First-aid kit, First-aid kit! Burn, Burn, Burn!

38
00:01:54.934 --> 00:02:02.782
Cut, Cut, Cut! Bruise, Bruise, Bruise! Sprain, Sprain, Sprain! Fall over, Fall over!

39
00:02:03.082 --> 00:02:05.595
Clap, clap! Great chanting!

40
00:02:06.583 --> 00:02:28.670
Accidents happen! Dara's brother fell over while he was running and got a sprain and a bruise. Their mum got a small burn while she was cooking. Sokha got a cut on his hand. Luckily, they have a first-aid kit at home. In a serious accident, you must make an ambulance call: the emergency number in Cambodia is 119.

41
00:02:28.970 --> 00:02:31.271
I love this story, Ms. Lily!

42
00:02:32.283 --> 00:02:34.831
What is it? Can you say it?

43
00:02:37.731 --> 00:02:39.687
Cut! Well done!

44
00:02:40.683 --> 00:02:42.929
What is it? Can you say it?

45
00:02:45.829 --> 00:02:48.075
First-aid kit! Well done!

46
00:02:49.083 --> 00:02:51.654
What is it? Can you say it?

47
00:02:54.554 --> 00:02:56.731
Fall over! Well done!

48
00:02:57.717 --> 00:02:59.461
Let's say it together!

49
00:02:59.761 --> 00:03:01.795
He fell over while he was running.

50
00:03:02.595 --> 00:03:03.887
Your turn!

51
00:03:07.387 --> 00:03:09.665
He fell over while he was running.

52
00:03:10.650 --> 00:03:12.928
What should you do if someone gets hurt?

53
00:03:16.228 --> 00:03:18.309
He fell over while he was running.

54
00:03:18.609 --> 00:03:19.854
Great answer!

55
00:03:20.850 --> 00:03:24.930
Today's value is safety. Be careful near cars and roads.

56
